{"id": "EUVD-2026-59013", "enisaUuid": "25722b71-8783-3eff-9bf3-1e0b58883ad0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: ip6_vti: require CAP_NET_ADMIN in the device netns for changelink\n\nvti6_changelink() operates on at most two netns, dev_net(dev) and the\ntunnel link netns t->net. They differ once the device is created in or\nmoved to a netns other than the one the request runs in. The rtnl\nchangelink path checks CAP_NET_ADMIN only against dev_net(dev), so a\ncaller privileged there but not in t->net can rewrite a tunnel that\nlives in t->net.\n\nGate vti6_changelink() on rtnl_dev_link_net_capable() at its top,\nbefore any attribute is parsed.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:52:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:19:25", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5254e7766b4ac02b66b2ccef896cd278503cb11", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef897249dc957089e6f7f11ceea699e093ad51bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f6e8b52a2cb3bbd72ddc2d44e474b907b9dcf5ba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c64b9ae7eb97e81d54b792910a3aeafd92566c79", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2b61c540571b3cc2f461e2a579ba2cc8c2a52cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b2f9c908f930ec4be17d389723f9a202d6a883c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f97e93ebf2f9b8ef3b87f7a9371255e84d151587", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2ac3b242c37dff323a964962e43854f4b1a2b79"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v9vm-v4fg-5x9v", "CVE-2026-72055"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "000bc0e8-cda5-305b-b026-0eb3415cf671", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "61220ab349485d911083d0b7990ccd3db6c63297 <b2b61c540571b3cc2f461e2a579ba2cc8c2a52cf"}, {"id": "0d600d53-690b-30af-aaf4-1f3bfc723090", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "1fcfdc